cff-version: 1.2.0
title: RTL8852CE Bluetooth/Wi-Fi Coexistence Toolkit for Linux
message: >-
  If you use this work in your research, debugging, or derivative
  patches, please cite it using this metadata.
authors:
  - family-names: Gouda
    given-names: Hamza
    email: hraafat357@gmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/hamza-gouda1/rtl8852ce-bt-coex"
abstract: >-
  Instrumented rtw89 driver patches, a correlated capture harness, and
  repair tooling for the Realtek RTL8852CE combo card on Linux, where the
  Wi-Fi/Bluetooth coexistence handshake does not complete (BT firmware
  reports coex version 0, AFH never engages, ~50% of coordination mailbox
  messages are rejected), causing Bluetooth A2DP audio packet loss under
  2.4 GHz Wi-Fi traffic. Includes a direct-HCI adaptive-frequency-hopping
  workaround and live coex policy tuning, and (v1.0) a persistent
  AFH guard service plus a PipeWire AAC codec build that together
  eliminate the audible stutter.
keywords:
  - linux
  - bluetooth
  - wifi
  - rtw89
  - realtek
  - coexistence
  - a2dp
  - kernel
